test_command=for t in tests/*_test.sh; do sh "$t" || exit 1; done
id=bump460-01 result=green reason=tests/bump460_test.sh, 11 tests green: test_bump460_01_version_agrees_with_newest_entry + test_bump460_01_version_newline_terminated_only_content (VERSION is a semver agreeing with the newest topmost entry, never a pinned literal, its only content the value plus one trailing newline), test_bump460_01_460_section_topmost_above_450 (exactly one dated '## [4.6.0] - 2026-09-13' heading, topmost, above [4.5.0] which stays above [4.4.0], Keep-a-Changelog preamble intact), test_bump460_01_entry_uses_existing_style (### Added/### Changed headings, bold lead-in bullets), content tests per fix group (entry_describes_specifier_conventions: two-digit index sequential from 01, one e2e-qa.feature per change dir, README per-sub-spec sections with relevant files + declared kebab-case destination domain, verifier per-domain file rule with create-when-new; entry_describes_coder_mechanical_checks: literal-grep id search in the project's test files, fixed plan threshold more-than-8-steps/more-than-1-shared-contract; entry_describes_verifier_code_present: mechanical code-present grep-or-receipt-existence, existence only never contents; entry_describes_orchestrator_bounded_slug: at-most-40 state=bad_slug limit with the pinned collision rules; entry_describes_probe_alignment_with_test_and_spec_updates: hyphen-free feature portion, foreign-id mismatch, tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh rewrite and spdd/specs/receipts.md update; entry_describes_surrounding_pin_moves: prompts-05/closingblock-05 gated retirements, roles-03 re-scope, the new suites), test_bump460_01_earlier_entries_byte_untouched ([4.5.0] still above [4.4.0] still describing its changes, the [4.5.0]-down tail byte-identical to git HEAD)
id=bump460-02 result=green reason=tests/bump460_test.sh, 5 tests green: test_bump460_02_entry_grades_minor_with_justification (entry grades as **minor**, not patch and not major, naming the justification: the specifier's conventions, coder's threshold and search, verifier's code-present and domain-file rules, and orchestrator's slug bullet are changes to rendered agent bodies and the probe's extraction behavior changes — not wording-only; naming the survivors: workflow contract, antz:generated marker format, access model, directory layout, install locations, no consumer breaks), test_bump460_02_entry_states_install_sh_untouched_re_render_carries_bump (install.sh itself untouched, bump reaches installed copies only through the normal ./install.sh --all re-render), test_bump460_02_entry_states_no_role_creates_v460_tag (no role creates the v4.6.0 tag — the human's commit-time follow-up, created against the human's bump commit, not pushed automatically), test_bump460_02_install_sh_byte_untouched_vs_head + test_bump460_02_no_v460_tag_created_while_uncommitted (both enforced live while the bump is uncommitted — install.sh matches HEAD, no v4.6.0 tag exists; the stacking-robust change_pending gate retires them loudly after the human's commit)
